"2025-09-18","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IN"},{"bioguideId":"G000553","fullName":"Rep. Green, Al [D-TX-9]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-23","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"F000477","fullName":"Rep. Foushee, Valerie P. [D-NC-4]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-23","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NC"},{"bioguideId":"Q000023","fullName":"Rep. Quigley, Mike [D-IL-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"S000185","fullName":"Rep. Scott, Robert C. \"Bobby\" [D-VA-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-22","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"W000831","fullName":"Rep. Walkinshaw, James R. [D-VA-11]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-13","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"VA"},{"bioguideId":"B001315","fullName":"Rep. Budzinski, Nikki [D-IL-13]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-19","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IL"},{"bioguideId":"R000606","fullName":"Rep. Raskin, Jamie [D-MD-8]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"MD"},{"bioguideId":"F000462","fullName":"Rep. Frankel, Lois [D-FL-22]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"D","sponsorshipDate":"2026-05-29","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"FL"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T14:42:22+00:00","id":"hr5449-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-18","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-18","text":"Referred to the House Committee on the Judiciary."},"laws":[],"number":"5449","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"L000397","district":18,"fullName":"Rep. Lofgren, Zoe [D-CA-18]","party":"D","state":"CA"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-09-18","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Redistricting Reform Act of </strong><strong>2025</strong></p><p>This bill sets forth requirements for congressional redistricting&nbsp;and generally prohibits mid-decade redistricting.</p><p>Specifically, the bill requires that congressional redistricting be conducted in accordance&nbsp;with a plan developed by (1) a state-established independent commission; or (2) if such a commission does not enact a plan, a three-judge panel from a U.S. District Court. This requirement does not apply to a state that has a plan developed and approved by an independent redistricting commission that complies with specified requirements.</p><p>The bill outlines the criteria for a redistricting plan, including that congressional districts must be drawn to (1) ensure the practical ability of a protected group to participate in the political process, nominate candidates, and elect representatives of choice; and (2) represent communities of interest and neighborhoods.</p><p>Additionally, the bill prohibits the use of a redistricting plan that was drawn with the intent (or has the effect of) materially favoring or disfavoring any political party.</p><p>Further, the bill establishes the requirements for appointing members to a state-established independent redistricting commission, including diversity requirements. The Government Accountability Office must report on the extent to which these commissions meet the diversity requirements.</p><p>The bill includes a provision to prevent states from redistricting more than once following an apportionment (i.e., mid-decade redistricting).</p><p>The bill also directs the Election Assistance Commission to make payments to states to carry out congressional redistricting.</p>","updateDate":"2026-07-23T19:17:13Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Redistricting Reform Act of 2025","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:40:56Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:40:56Z"}
